    "reason": "The US Smart Promotion Project was launched in early H1 2026 as a strategic priority. The project aims to establish a unified merchant charging and subsidy system, improving the merchant experience while increasing platform subsidy efficiency for a win-win outcome.\nSince launch in 2026, the charging side has achieved 75%+ GMV coverage and contributed 7%+ incremental GMV, exceeding both targets.\n\nKey Achievements:\nBuilt a unified merchant charging platform: Enabled merchants to enroll once and participate in multiple platform subsidy programs across daily operations, channels, and major campaigns. The team also continued to enhance the merchant data dashboard, helping merchants better understand the actual benefits of each program.\nDefined and optimized the subsidy tool strategy: Established a clear strategy across Platform Vouchers, RIV Vouchers, and Product Subsidies, supporting GMV growth during mid-year campaigns. Key innovations included segmented high-value voucher strategies, the first launch of highly personalized RIV Vouchers, and supply-selection-driven product subsidy strategies.\nImproved subsidy efficiency measurement: Continuously refined ROAS measurement methodologies to accelerate strategy iteration, including the Capped ROAS methodology, Bootstrap CUPED variance reduction, Libra pre-AA alert mechanism, and Seedfinder to reduce pre-AA variance.",
