    "reason": "The POP Spring Festival Project was launched to stabilize business performance during the holiday period and accelerate post-holiday recovery in February. Facing pressure from holiday-driven supply fluctuations, lower merchant operating intent, and a short marketing gap in early February, the project focused on keeping merchants active, sustaining content supply, and ensuring business momentum across the full month.\n\nThe campaign delivered clear business impact. During the campaign period, POP GMV improved by 8% compared with the pre-campaign period, while Spring Festival GMV grew 160% year-over-year, outperforming the broader US market. The project helped POP move from below-target progress before the campaign to full-month target completion above 100%. It also captured post-holiday demand opportunities, with high-AOV categories such as furniture achieving nearly 90% uplift, while merchant co-investment and advertising participation supported margin improvement.\n\nThis result was enabled by fast cross-functional execution across marketing, merchant operations, creator/content, product operations and advertising teams. The team compressed the usual campaign preparation cycle into two weeks, aligned strategy and resources quickly, and combined POP-owned activities with platform campaigns to maintain traffic and operating rhythm throughout the month. By pre-building content supply, driving merchant sign-ups, securing holiday pricing and supply, and introducing incentive mechanisms linked to merchant content and ad investment, the project kept merchant participation active during a traditionally slow period.\n\nBeyond the February result, the project also established a repeatable holiday operating playbook for POP, covering pre-holiday sampling, ad recharge, price and supply commitment, scheduled content posting, and merchant incentive mechanisms. This created a more structured approach for future holiday operations and supported continued business stability during later holiday periods.",
